{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3284-771f-a1d8-f8a2dcf49cd8","id":"01a1a63e-0b79-7621-b3d8-c6b75dc4be1a","idempotency_key":"d0d10e1ba9cff1cbca9c246ec1207bb20264d78a9b8df63d4d9a6ae6b9e77dcd","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:07:26Z","payload":{"note":"Three of five done, two honestly blocked. Done: i-7ba0 (keyring/redaction audit), i-ac0a (no key in DB/log/context/fixture - the mock server now records headers, which is what makes the header-versus-body claim checkable), i-60af (permission/approval bypass tests). New file crates/ai/tests/security.rs, 10 tests, plus docs/security.md recording the audit and the parts that are NOT verified. Two corrected assumptions worth keeping: write_note is a BOARD write and is legitimately allowed during Play - the tools the policy refuses in a game are the structural study writes (create_study, add_chapter), so 'study writes are blocked' does not mean all writing is; and ToolRegistry::default() is empty, the specs live behind builtin(). BLOCKED: i-23d6 (MCP auth/resource traversal) and i-5896 (destructive action review) cannot be demonstrated - there is no MCP server yet (t-745d) and no destructive tool exists in the builtin registry, so the destructive-scope test returns early rather than pretending to pass.","target":"t-69c9"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
