{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3284-771f-a1d8-f8a2dcf49cd8","id":"01a1a64b-e9d8-73e1-856b-40f6de4bb5f9","idempotency_key":"143352b06399572f2d6f472c29dac8b245aebaba46a051b5d940786712268bae","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:22:35Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-5896","note":"Reviewed every path that changes stored content: board writes are policy-gated then revision-checked; MCP writes return approval_required and run nothing; study content needs a scope never granted to MCP by default; locked/published boards refuse and offer a copy; an approval answers once. No Destructive tool exists yet, said plainly rather than counted as a pass. Table in docs/security.md.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-69c9/i-5896"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3284-771f-a1d8-f8a2dcf49cd8","id":"01a1a64b-e9f2-7764-b459-32a3eff2f34c","idempotency_key":"50bbc0bfcecabe66d59685c3d192ed2910aee2f5811f28c7870e64602fb564ab","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:22:35Z","payload":{"note":"All five now. The two that were blocked became demonstrable once t-745d landed the server: i-23d6 is five app tests (token matching including near-miss and scheme-only; rbc:// traversal attempts - ../, absolute paths, file://, foreign schemes, over-long shapes - all resolving to nothing while a real board uri still reads; the rate limiter refusing past its cap) and i-5896 is a review table of every path that changes stored content. Worth recording in the review itself: MCP tools/call was originally calling the host DIRECTLY, bypassing the policy entirely - found while writing t-851f, now routed through decide() with Origin::Mcp. That is the finding the review existed to catch and it came from the review, not from luck.","target":"t-69c9"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
