{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3284-771f-a1d8-f8a2dcf49cd8","id":"01a1a64c-1e03-7568-88fb-b7d86589e050","idempotency_key":"1a259727f9033864fa4394798230407f2d1a237b8fe6ca55554208bd1a0a0e84","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:22:48Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-7ba0","note":"Keyring/redaction audit: no credential is persisted anywhere. api_key lives in ProviderConfig in memory and is used only to build the Authorization header; every set_setting call site was read and none writes a token; the only 'token' in rbc-db is an SAN token in update_moves. Redaction is asserted by the_key_never_appears_in_an_error (including Debug, which is what a log writes) and the_key_travels_in_the_authorization_header_and_not_in_the_body, which drives a real HTTP request at the mock server. See docs/security.md.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-69c9/i-7ba0"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
